<body><div class="app"><aside class="sidebar"><a class="brand" href="#home"><span class="brand-symbol">✳</span><span>APLI<small>NATURE EXPLORER</small></span></a><div class="side-label">EXPLORE</div><nav aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="#home" data-nav="home" class="nav active"><span>⌂</span> Overview</a><a href="#identify" data-nav="identify" class="nav"><span>◎</span> Identify a species</a><a href="#collection" data-nav="collection" class="nav"><span>▦</span> My collection</a><a href="#fieldguide" data-nav="fieldguide" class="nav"><span>◈</span> Field guide</a><a href="#about" data-nav="about" class="nav"><span>ⓘ</span> About APLI</a></nav><div class="side-bottom"><div class="mini-icon">🌿</div><strong>Adventure awaits.</strong><p>Every discovery starts with a little curiosity.</p><a href="#identify" class="side-cta">Start exploring ↗</a></div><div class="side-foot">APLI · EARLY PROTOTYPE v0.1</div></aside>
<main class="main"><header class="topbar"><div class="breadcrumb">APLI <span>/</span> <b id="pageLabel">Overview</b></div><div class="top-actions"><span class="status-dot"></span><span>Explorer mode</span><span class="avatar">EX</span></div></header>
<section id="home" class="page shown"><div class="hero"><div class="hero-content"><span class="eyebrow">✦ WELCOME TO THE WILD</span><h1>A world of wonder,<br><em>right outside.</em></h1><p>Discover plants and animals around you, learn amazing facts, and turn every outdoor adventure into a new achievement.</p><a class="btn light" href="#identify">Start a discovery <span>↗</span></a></div><div class="hero-art" aria-hidden="true"><div class="orbit orbit1"></div><div class="orbit orbit2"></div><div class="hero-leaf one">✳</div><div class="hero-leaf two">✿</div><div class="hero-leaf three">❋</div><div class="hero-illustration">🦋</div><div class="floating-tag">✦ + XP for every discovery</div></div></div><div class="section-head"><div><span class="overline">YOUR JOURNEY SO FAR</span><h2>Explorer dashboard</h2></div><span class="subtle">Your progress is saved on this device</span></div><div class="stats"><div class="stat"><div class="stat-icon lavender">✿</div><div><div class="stat-number" id="speciesCount">0</div><div class="stat-label">Species discovered</div></div></div><div class="stat"><div class="stat-icon lime">✦</div><div><div class="stat-number" id="xpCount">0</div><div class="stat-label">Total experience points</div></div></div><div class="stat"><div class="stat-icon peach">◈</div><div><div class="stat-number" id="rankCount">Seedling</div><div class="stat-label">Explorer rank</div></div></div></div><div class="section-head space"><div><span class="overline">WHAT'S NEXT?</span><h2>Your next adventure</h2></div></div><div class="two-col"><a href="#identify" class="action-card"><div class="action-visual pale-green">📸</div><div><span class="small-tag">01 · DISCOVER</span><h3>Found something interesting?</h3><p>Upload a photo and get a starting clue to what it could be.</p><b>Identify a species ↗</b></div></a><a href="#collection" class="action-card"><div class="action-visual pale-purple">🪴</div><div><span class="small-tag">02 · COLLECT</span><h3>Build your nature collection</h3><p>Save your discoveries, earn XP, and grow your explorer rank.</p><b>View collection ↗</b></div></a></div><div class="tip"><span>☀</span><div><strong>Nature note</strong><p>Take photos from a safe distance. Leave plants, animals, and habitats as you found them.</p></div></div></section>
<section id="identify" class="page"><div class="page-heading"><span class="overline">START A DISCOVERY</span><h1>Identify a species<span class="accent">.</span></h1><p>Upload a picture from your APLI device, phone, or camera. We'll generate image clues, then you can verify and save your find.</p></div><div class="identify-grid"><div class="panel"><div class="panel-top"><h3>01 / Add a photo</h3><span class="pill">JPG · PNG · WEBP</span></div><label for="photo" class="upload" id="dropZone"><div id="uploadPlaceholder"><div class="upload-icon">↥</div><h3>Drop your photo here</h3><p>or click to browse files</p><span class="upload-help">The photo stays on your device during image classification</span></div><img id="preview" alt="Selected species photo" hidden></label><input id="photo" type="file" accept="image/*" hidden><button class="btn dark full" id="analyzeBtn" disabled>Analyze photo <span>✦</span></button><p class="fineprint">Experimental AI hints use a general image classifier, not a specialist wildlife identification system. Always verify species before saving.</p></div><div class="panel"><div class="panel-top"><h3>02 / Verify your find</h3><span class="pill">YOUR DISCOVERY</span></div><div id="analysisStatus" class="analysis-status">Add a photo to see possible image labels here.</div><div id="guesses" class="guesses"></div><label class="field-label" for="speciesSearch">Search for the actual species</label><input id="speciesSearch" class="field" type="search" placeholder="e.g. Black-capped Chickadee" autocomplete="off"><div id="suggestions" class="suggestions" role="listbox"></div><div id="selectedSpecies" class="selected-species" hidden></div><label class="field-label" for="notes">Field notes <span>(optional)</span></label><textarea id="notes" class="field" rows="3" placeholder="Where did you see it? What was it doing?"></textarea><button class="btn green full" id="saveBtn" disabled>Save to my collection <span>↗</span></button><p class="fineprint">Species information comes from iNaturalist when available. Rarity and XP are game rewards, not conservation assessments.</p></div></div></section>
<section id="collection" class="page"><div class="page-heading heading-row"><div><span class="overline">YOUR DIGITAL FIELD JOURNAL</span><h1>My collection<span class="accent">.</span></h1><p>Every discovery tells a story. Here's yours.</p></div><button class="btn outline" id="exportBtn">Export collection ↓</button></div><div class="collection-summary"><strong id="collectionSummary">0 discoveries</strong><span id="collectionXP">0 XP earned</span></div><div id="collectionGrid" class="collection-grid"></div><div id="emptyCollection" class="empty-state"><div>🌱</div><h3>Your collection is ready to grow.</h3><p>Head outdoors, take a photo, and record your first find!</p><a class="btn green" href="#identify">Make a discovery ↗</a></div></section>
<section id="fieldguide" class="page"><div class="page-heading"><span class="overline">LOOK CLOSER</span><h1>Field guide<span class="accent">.</span></h1><p>Search living things by name and explore their taxonomy through iNaturalist.</p></div><div class="panel guide-panel"><label for="guideSearch" class="field-label">Search for a plant or animal</label><input id="guideSearch" class="field" type="search" placeholder="Try: monarch butterfly, red fox, dandelion" autocomplete="off"><p class="fineprint">Search results require an internet connection.</p><div id="guideResults" class="guide-results"></div></div><div class="tip"><span>✿</span><div><strong>Every species has a role</strong><p>Whether it's a common dandelion or a rarely spotted bird, each part of your local ecosystem matters.</p></div></div></section>
<section id="about" class="page"><div class="page-heading"><span class="overline">THE STORY BEHIND THE PROJECT</span><h1>Meet APLI<span class="accent">.</span></h1><p>Animals and Plants Logger and Identifier</p></div><div class="about-hero"><div><span class="eyebrow">OUR MISSION</span><h2>More moments in nature.<br>More curiosity about our world.</h2><p>APLI is an educational prototype designed to encourage children aged 7–11 to spend more time outdoors, notice local biodiversity, and learn through playful discovery.</p></div><span>🌎</span></div><div class="about-cols"><div class="panel"><span class="overline">HOW IT WORKS</span><h3>From camera to collection</h3><p>The proposed APLI device captures photos outdoors. Later, an app helps identify plants and animals and awards playful experience points for discoveries. This website is an early version of the app experience.</p></div><div class="panel"><span class="overline">THE EXPERIMENT</span><h3>Can exploration change habits?</h3><p>The proposed study compares three 3-day phases: without APLI, with APLI, and without APLI again, tracking reported outdoor time and device screen time. No study results are claimed here.</p></div></div><div class="tip"><span>⚑</span><div><strong>Prototype limitation</strong><p>This website cannot connect to a Raspberry Pi automatically, identify all species reliably, or sync users across devices. A future version can add specialized species recognition, hardware integration, and a consent-based data system.</p></div></div></section>
